    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173-a2">

                <pb facs="0282" n="194" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg194"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to
                            Prince Ch’ing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-07-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Imperial Highness</hi>: On June 27 last, by
                    direction of my Government, I had the honor to address a note to your imperial
                    highness inquiring what guaranties of early action and satifactory conclusion of
                    the work China would give in case the signatory powers agreed to accept the new
                    proposals of the Chinese Government concerning the Whangpu conservancy matter.
                    To this I have as yet received no reply.</p>
                <p>In order that I may inform my Government, I regret that I am obliged to again ask
                    your imperial highness for the courtesy of an early reply.</p>
                <p>I also avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
